Hello David,

X  is a resident at 585 Corydon ave. I have included him in this email.

He has been a resident here since X and he was not provided with the
storage unit despite a unit existing that was clearly marked #6 correlated
with his suite. Storage was not included in his lease agreement but the
Landlord has attempted to persuade me that the unit I have has been
provided as a 'courtesy' to me which has been subsequently recognized as a
service provided as they have since given me notice that they are
withdrawing the service of storage unit and I will be receiving a rent
decrease based on this, This should be extended to X as she was denied the
service on the basis of avoiding following RTB protocol that would have
resulted in necessitating rent decrease.

In addition, X has also been offered laundry service renovation which he
has refused. On May 1 laundry services will be withdrawn and this will
necessitate a reduction in his rent as well.

Please note that my charge is that Thorwin Properties has practiced
deception and fraud in denying X access to the storage locker in order to
deceitfully avoid following RTB procedure which should result in rent
decrease.

The landlord has engaged in lies and exploitation of both tenant and RTB
and this must be addressed as soon as possible.

All the best,
Evan Rosner


